Third-party programs bundled with the macOS application
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Crisp's own source code is Apache-2.0. The shipped macOS application additionally
bundles the third-party programs below. They are NOT linked into Crisp: each is a
separate executable that Crisp launches as a subprocess, so each remains under its
own licence and Crisp's Apache-2.0 licence does not extend to them.

The full licence text for each ships inside the application bundle at
`Contents/Resources/engine/licenses/`, staged by `apps/desktop/Scripts/vendor.sh`.

FFmpeg 8.1.1 (ffmpeg, ffprobe)
    https://ffmpeg.org
    GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
    IMPORTANT: the vendored build is configured `--enable-gpl --enable-version3`,
    which makes GPLv3 the operative licence for these binaries, not the LGPL that
    a default FFmpeg build carries. Bundled licence:
    engine/licenses/ffmpeg-COPYING.GPLv3.txt
    Source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg at tag n8.1.1.
    Binaries vendored from https://ffmpeg.martin-riedl.de (pinned + SHA-256 checked).

whisper.cpp v1.9.0 (whisper-cli)
    https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
    MIT License. Built from the pinned tag by Scripts/vendor.sh.
    Bundled licence: engine/licenses/whisper.cpp-LICENSE.txt

CPython 3.13 (python-build-standalone runtime)
    https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone
    Python Software Foundation License Version 2.
    Bundled licence: engine/licenses/python-LICENSE.txt

Note on platform scope: these binaries are macOS-only. iOS and iPadOS cannot spawn
subprocesses at all, so the Apple mobile builds ship none of them and use
AVFoundation and Core ML instead.

